  "skills": [
    {
      "stage": "formation",
      "id": "4075c246d85f033248397fd90d1d3e2a68c1d0ed16bd69acc9df79c604b50c9f",
      "content": {
        "applicability": [
          "Adapter/handler code where a client-supplied optional override can be omitted or null and a documented default/preset should be restored",
          "Tasks phrased as 'restore documented preset behavior' while keeping client-supplied values and output format compatible",
          "Small service entry points (e.g., request dict lookups feeding a response dict or plan/manifest) with a DEFAULT-style constant present"
        ],
        "change_summary": "Created skill from four runs where handlers passed a None/omitted client override straight through instead of substituting the documented preset. All runs fixed the pattern with a null-check fallback to the named default, kept client-supplied values, and passed public tests. One run shows a redundant double-check diff that still passed, so verification includes a simplification check. Skill captures the reusable diagnosis, verification, and exclusion (don't rewrite format) without copying task-specific values.",
        "counterexamples": [
          "Two different-looking fixes both passed public tests in these runs; passing tests alone does not prove one form is better, only that the semantic (null -> default) is satisfied.",
          "Run 27c55838bc73cd8556a35cfdcf378fd0 shipped a redundant duplicate conditional and still passed; public tests passing does not certify code cleanliness.",
          "If omitted and explicit null must map to different values, or the preset lives in nested/serialized structures, this simple fallback pattern does not apply."
        ],
        "evidence_refs": [
          "d3db6566528a39247af26465f0933bdd",
          "69dddec2adaeb066a30c0d15dffa0c2a",
          "27c55838bc73cd8556a35cfdcf378fd0",
          "8bc523660ae6989faaac71432e8676d3"
        ],
        "exclusions": [
          "Do not apply when the spec requires distinguishing an omitted key from an explicit null (use sentinel/FIELD-in-request checks instead).",
          "Do not apply when the expected value is not a literal constant default (e.g., computed per-request or dependent on other fields).",
          "Do not rewrite output formatting, add fields, or change error handling beyond the defaulting fix.",
          "Do not default falsy values (0, empty string, False) unless the issue text explicitly says so."
        ],
        "name": "restore-default-on-null-override",
        "parent": null,
        "steps": [
          "Locate the handler that reads the client override from the request and note where the value flows into the response.",
          "Identify the documented default constant or preset already defined in the code or README; do not invent a new literal.",
          "Check how the issue treats omission vs explicit null; if both should yield the default, an 'is None' check covers both, since a missing key typically surfaces as None via dict.get.",
          "Insert a minimal null fallback (conditional reassignment or conditional expression) at the point the raw override is used.",
          "Preserve all client-supplied non-null values exactly and keep the existing output format unchanged.",
          "Simplify the guard to a single null check; avoid duplicated conditions (one observed fix repeated the same 'is not None' test redundantly, which passed tests but adds needless complexity).",
          "Run the public test command before submitting."
        ],
        "verification": [
          "Run the public test command and confirm it passes after the edit.",
          "Trace each case: key omitted, key set to null, key set to a client value — confirm default, default, and client value respectively.",
          "Confirm no falsy-but-valid client values (0, '', False) are overridden by the default.",
          "Confirm the response structure and serialization are byte-identical to the pre-patch format for non-null inputs."
        ]
      },
      "evidence_hash": "eb7483c5507a6080cb5c3c63581486a2d7e7accebca36874b564cdbdd9d1e82d",
